      "source_number": "760",
      "independent_solution": "Six domains over the real numbers. (a) (12y-1)/y requires y!=0, so R\\{0}. (b) (3x+1)/(15x-4) requires 15x-4!=0, so R\\{4/15}. (c) (13x+7)/(2|x|-6) excludes |x|=3, hence both -3 and +3: R\\{-3,3}. (d) 4|x|+8>=8>0 for every real x, hence (3x^2-x)/(4|x|+8) has domain R, including 0. Numerator zeros are allowed and do not restrict any of (a)-(d). (e) sqrt(6-2x) requires 6-2x>=0, hence x<=3, including x=3. (f) x^2+1>0 for all real x, so (5-x)/(x^2+1)>=0 iff 5-x>=0, hence x<=5, including x=5. The square-root nonnegative-radicand condition differs from a rational denominator's nonzero condition.",
